INSERT INTO `mod_lore_codex_entry` (`ID`, `Kind`, `Zone`, `SortOrder`, `Faction`, `RequiredState`, `Title`, `Body`, `Sources`) VALUES
(21000, 0, 210, 0, 0, 13, 'Icecrown', 'Icecrown is the frozen crown of Northrend and the Lich King''s own domain. Over it rises Icecrown Citadel, the seat of the master of the Scourge, who was once Arthas Menethil, prince of Lordaeron. The land around the citadel is his fortress. Three great gates, Mord''rethar, Aldur''thar and Corp''rethar, bar the road to its walls, the Cult of the Damned serves at his gates and in his cathedral, and the vrykul of Jotunheim fight one another for the honor of joining his chosen at Ymirheim. Every power that would see him ended has come. The Argent Crusade has broken through the southeastern mountains, the Knights of the Ebon Blade strike from Death''s Rise and from smaller camps across the glacier, and the gunships Skybreaker and Orgrim''s Hammer hang above the battlefield, where the Alliance and the Horde fight the Scourge and each other. In the far west, the last of the Scarlet Onslaught holds a harbor of its own.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Icecrown (Lich King''s domain, Icecrown Citadel); quest 13036 reward text (where the Alliance and the Horde failed, the Crusade broke in); quests 13237, 13315, 13316 (the gates on the road to the citadel); quest 12938 reward text (Jotunheim vrykul ascend to the Ymirjar); quests 13224, 13225 (the gunships); npc_text 13525-13529 (Onslaught at the harbor below Death''s Rise); quest 13667 description (the tournament); mod-individual-progression: tournament areas phased from state 15 (checkIPPhasing, ipp_aware_npcs.sql ''-- Argent Tournament''); quest 13364 description (the Cult''s Cathedral of Darkness); quests 13106, 13155 (Ebon Blade camps at Blackwatch and the Rise of Suffering)'),
(21001, 1, 210, 1, 0, 13, 'The Argent Vanguard', 'The Argent Vanguard is the Argent Crusade''s walled camp in the southeastern reaches of Icecrown, raised where the Crusade forced its way into the Lich King''s land after the Alliance and the Horde had failed. Highlord Tirion Fordring commands here, and the camp is under siege. Nerubians of the Forgotten Depths swarm through the Valley of Echoes to the west, where captured crusaders lie webbed on the field as living shields. In the Vanguard Infirmary at the camp''s heart Father Gustav fights a venom no one can cure, and Penumbrius of the bronze dragonflight keeps the proto-drakes that fly for the Crusade.', 'quest 13036 reward text (where both failed, the Crusade succeeded; now on the defensive); quest 13226 description (southeastern reaches of Icecrown); quests 13008, 13039, 13040 (nerubians of the Forgotten Depths, crusaders as living shields, incurable venom); quests 13044, 13045 (Penumbrius, proto-brood, Vanguard Infirmary at the center); npc_text 13797 (Penumbrius of the bronze dragonflight); spell_area 57673 (Chapter I, phase 2) in 4501 and 4504 until DONE 13070/13086; phase 2 spawns: Tirion 28179, Entari, Dalfors, Gustav 30226, Penumbrius 30227, Webbed Crusaders 30268/30273'),
(21002, 1, 210, 2, 0, 13, 'Scourgeholme and the Breach', 'Beyond the Valley of Echoes, the Breach is the gap the Argent Crusade blew through the mountain wall, and past it lies Scourgeholme, the first Scourge encampment within Icecrown. It is a Nerubian stronghold of the Forgotten Depths, raised in tiers: Salranax the Flesh Render lords over the temple on the first, High Priest Yath''amon preaches at the spirit tower on the second, and Underking Talonox holds court in the Pit of Fiends up the high road. The Crusade charged in when the wall came down and was thrown back, leaving many soldiers behind, and the Lich King himself has been seen among its defenders.', 'quest 13008 description (blew a hole in the side of the mountain, charged into Scourgeholme, overwhelmed); quest 13044 description (first Scourge encampment in Icecrown; soldiers left behind); quest 13125 description (the three lords and where they keep); creature 30443 The Lich King, phaseMask 2, at 6698,584 in Scourgeholme (Chapter I phase); zone_areas 4506: Forgotten Depths high priests, underkings, Captured Crusader 30407'),
(21003, 1, 210, 3, 0, 13, 'Crusaders'' Pinnacle', 'Crusaders'' Pinnacle is a high crag above the Breach, named by the Scourge in mockery of the Argent crusaders whose skulls they piled upon it. The land falls away from it toward Scourgeholme and the heart of Icecrown, and whoever holds its height holds a foothold inside the very walls of the Lich King''s domain. The Crusade has not forgotten what was done to its dead there.', 'quest 13141 description (an area the Scourge mockingly named Crusaders'' Pinnacle; skulls of fallen brethren); quest 13157 description (inside the walls of Icecrown); creature_text 31003 group 0 (look at what they''ve done to our people)'),
(21004, 1, 210, 4, 0, 13, 'Onslaught Harbor and Death''s Rise', 'Off Icecrown''s western coast the Scarlet Onslaught holds an island harbor, manned by battle-hardened veterans of New Hearthglen in the Dragonblight. Guards, paladins and raven bishops walk its docks, the Crimson Cathedral has a single, heavily guarded entrance, and gryphon riders patrol the sky, while two ships ride at anchor under Captains Welsington and Hartford. On the cliff above stands Death''s Rise, where the Knights of the Ebon Blade under Lord-Commander Arete mean to end the Onslaught once and for all, though the Argent Crusade turns a blind eye to it. His knights raise the Scarlet dead into the very thing they hated, ride bone gryphons made from captured Onslaught mounts, and search the enemy''s trunks for each day''s plans.', 'npc_text 13525-13530 (Arete''s tale: the remnant from New Hearthglen, end the Onslaught once and for all); quest 12807 reward text (the Argent Crusade turns a blind eye; the Ebon Blade will be their end); quests 12810, 12813, 12814, 12815, 12838 (blood ritual, tincture, bone gryphons, intel trunks); quests 12840, 12847 (captains on the ships; the Crimson Cathedral''s single guarded entrance); zone_areas 4417: Onslaught Harbor Guard, Paladin, Raven Bishop, Gryphon Rider, Captains 29489/29490; quest 12806 description (Death''s Rise overlooking the sea along the cliff wall)'),
(21005, 1, 210, 5, 0, 13, 'The Shadow Vault', 'The Shadow Vault is a Scourge stronghold cut into the mountains of northern Icecrown, where the death knight General Lightsbane oversees the forging of new weapons. Above its spires floats the Ocular, an eye through which the Lich King watches over the vault. Cultists, geists and ravenous ghouls crowd its grounds and death knight masters keep its yards, while on its ledges and middle tier wait three of the Lich King''s servants: the abomination Vile, the banshee Lady Nightswood and a one-eyed geist called the Leaper.', 'quests 12887, 12892 descriptions (the Ocular floats above the vault''s spires and watches the area); quest 12896 description (General Lightsbane in the vault overseeing the creation of new weapons); quest 12893 description (the three on the ledges east and west and the mid-tier); quest 13069 (the Leaper''s single eye); spell_area 30181 (Phase Shift I, phase 2) in 4477 until DONE 12896 (Alliance) or 12897 (Horde); phase 2 spawns: Shadow Cultist, Vault Geist, Rabid Cannibal, Death Knight Master, Ocular 29747, Vile 29769, Nightswood 29770, Leaper 29840, Baron Sliver 29804'),
(21006, 1, 210, 6, 0, 13, 'Jotunheim', 'Jotunheim is a vrykul city over the mountains west of the Shadow Vault, where its people were first reawakened, a place second only to Ymirheim in their hearts. Its warriors are forever challenging one another to ascend: the victors go to Ymirheim to join the Lich King''s elite, and the losers are reduced to vargul. They spar on the Savage Ledge below the hall of Thane Ufrang the Mighty, fight with honor on Battlescar Spire and let ancient heroes slumber in the Halls of the Ancestors, while oracles in Kul''galar Keep scry through the Eye of the Lich King. Overthane Balargarde, master of Jotunheim, rules from his fortress on its southwestern edge.', 'quest 13084 reward text (first reawakened here; second only to Ymirheim); quest 12938 reward text (challenge to ascend; Ymirjar or vargul); quests 12939, 12943 (Savage Ledge sparring; Ufrang''s hall overlooks it); quest 13137 description (Battlescar Spire); quests 13121, 13133 (Kul''galar Keep oracles and the Eye of the Lich King; slumbering mjordin in the Halls of the Ancestors); quest 13142 description and creature_template 31016 subname Master of Jotunheim (Balargarde Fortress on the southwestern edge)'),
(21007, 1, 210, 7, 0, 13, 'Njorndar Village and the Underhalls', 'Njorndar Village lies in the southwest of greater Jotunheim, home to spear-sisters, water magi and the proto-drakes the vrykul ride to war. Beside it a water lock teems with elementals the magi have yet to tame, and in a cave on the village''s south side the bone witch throws her bones. To the northeast the Underhalls burrow into the mountain. There, by the Lich King''s leave, a mad scientist known as Dr. Terrible experiments on vargul, and a massive flesh giant stands still at the end of the Hall of Horrors. Below lies the Circle of Suffering, where Thane Illskar keeps his champions, and a vargul named Bethod Feigr broods alone on his shame.', 'zone_areas 4526: Njorndar Spear-Sister, Mjordin Water Magus, Njorndar Proto-Drake, The Bone Witch 30232; quest 13091 (water lock teeming with untamed elementals; the cave); quest 12999 (the cave on the south side of Njorndar); quest 13092 (bone witch and rune reader); quests 13042, 13043 (Dr. Terrible in the Underhalls to the northeast; Nergeld at the end of the Hall of Horrors); quest 13059 (Thane Illskar and his champions below in the Circle of Suffering); npc_text 13782 (Bethod: leave me to my shame)'),
(21008, 1, 210, 8, 0, 13, 'Valhalas', 'Valhalas is the vrykul''s sacred battle pit, north of Njorndar Village, where warriors fight for their ascendance and the corpses of the fallen stand as a testament to the strength of their ways. Those who prove unworthy are reduced to vargul. The val''kyr Geirrvif presides over its challenges, and from the southern lip the vrykul death knight Gjonner the Merciless looks on with open contempt for outsiders. Harpoon platforms overhang the cliffs on either side.', 'npc_text 13918 (Geirrvif: corpses a testament to the strength of our ways); quest 13059 (fight for ascendance in Valhalas); quest 13213 description and reward text (battle pit to the north; unworthy become vargul); quest 13214 reward text (the vrykul death knight Gjonner, southern lip); npc_text 13919 (Gjonner); quest 13069 (harpoon platforms on either side of Valhalas)'),
(21009, 1, 210, 9, 0, 13, 'The Weeping Quarry', 'The Weeping Quarry, down the path southwest of the Shadow Vault, is a Scourge saronite quarry worked without rest by risen laborers, who pull immense amounts of ore from the ground. Ghoul lookouts watch over the pits, plaguehounds kept starving to sharpen their temper prowl the paths, and crystals scattered through the camp seem to serve as its defenses, not unlike the ziggurats of other Scourge holdings. Where all that saronite goes is a question the Ebon Blade means to answer.', 'quests 13169, 13170, 13171 descriptions (saronite quarry to the southwest; starved plaguehounds; lookouts; crystals like ziggurats; immense amounts of ore); zone_areas 4517: Risen Laborer, Restless Lookout, Hungering Plaguehound, Containment Crystal'),
(21010, 1, 210, 10, 0, 13, 'Ymirheim', 'Ymirheim is the great frost vrykul city at the center of Icecrown, home of the Ymirjar, the vrykul the Lich King has deemed worthy to be his chosen. Val''kyr taskmistresses drive captives into the Saronite Mines beneath it, where an unknown voice whispers of fear and betrayal in the dark, blight falconers and proto-drakes hold the air, and automated spear guns inside the walls tear at anything that flies over. Alliance troops fight their way up the pass from the glacier to the east and the Kor''kron from the north, and both drop soldiers into the city from the air at heavy cost.', 'quests 13293, 13296 (big frost vrykul town in the middle of Icecrown); quests 13330, 13336 (the Ymirjar, those who gained the Lich King''s favor); quests 13300, 13302 (people captured and put to work in the saronite mines); spell_area 27769 (Whisper Gulch: Yogg-Saron Whisper) in 4514 with no conditions; creature_text 29881 An Unknown Voice (''They are coming for you'', ''Give in to your fear'', ''They have turned against you''); quests 13284, 13301, 13309, 13310 (ground assault from the glacier east and north; spear guns tearing up transports); zone_areas 4513: Val''kyr Taskmistress, Blight Falconer, Savage Proto-Drake, Ymirheim Spear Gun'),
(21011, 1, 210, 11, 0, 13, 'The Broken Front and Mord''rethar', 'Mord''rethar, the Death Gate, is the first of the gates that bar the road to Icecrown Citadel. Flesh giants on its ramparts hurl boulders and ice at anything below, and plague cauldrons simmer in its western chamber. The field before it is the Broken Front, strewn with slain soldiers and their discarded helms and armor. Dying men still lie among the dead, Alliance and Horde alike, while geists, necromancers and abominations raise the fallen to fight again.', 'quests 13237, 13287 (take each gate; the first); quest 13277 (flesh giants on the ramparts hurl boulders and ice); quest 13279 (plague cauldrons in the western chamber of the death gate); zone_areas 4507: Slain Alliance Soldier, Dying Soldier, Dying Berserker, Risen Alliance Soldier, Malefic Necromancer, Hulking Abomination, Abandoned Helm and Armor'),
(21012, 1, 210, 12, 0, 13, 'Aldur''thar and the Bombardment', 'Aldur''thar, the Desolation Gate, is the second gate on the road to the citadel, and the Cult of the Damned holds it. New initiates train at its southern end, an overseer runs each of its encampments, void summoners bind demonic minions in the north, and in the northwest cultists stir cauldrons of a brew that enslaves the will of every pledge who drinks it. Below the gate lies the Bombardment, where Scourge war machines, gargoyles and fleshrenders mass, and the Kor''kron hold the glacier''s edge north of Ymirheim.', 'quests 13315, 13351 (the gate of desolation; south, central, north and northwest regions); quests 13318, 13319, 13342, 13320 (initiates in the south; overseers; void summoners in the north; the cauldron brew that steals the will); zone_areas 4509: Scourge War Machine, Gargoyle Ambusher, Enraged Fleshrender, Kor''kron Infantry, Ground Commander Xutjja; quest 13340 (Xutjja''s troops at the edge of the glacier north of Ymirheim)'),
(21013, 1, 210, 13, 0, 13, 'The Valley of Lost Hope and Sindragosa''s Fall', 'The Valley of Lost Hope stretches below the gunships between Ymirheim and Sindragosa''s Fall, a valley of great strategic worth that crawls with decomposed ghouls, frostskull magi and bone giants, while scavenging geists pick apart the war machines left on the field. The Alliance holds a landing at its edge, and to the north lie the remains of an old army encampment. East beyond the valley, Sindragosa''s Fall may be a graveyard of the blue dragonflight. There the Cult of the Damned, closely watched by undead vrykul necrolords, raises frost wyrms of the dreaded Frostbrood from the bones of blue dragons.', 'quest 13304 description (the strategically important valley below us; demolisher in the southeastern corner); quest 13305 description (an old army encampment to the north); quests 13349, 13397 descriptions (Sindragosa''s Fall east beyond the valley; possibly a blue dragonflight graveyard; frostbrood raised from blue dragon bones; Cult under the vrykul lackeys); zone_areas 4537: Decomposed Ghoul, Frostskull Magus, Bone Giant, Scavenging Geist, Ground Commander Koup and Skybreaker Infantry'),
(21014, 1, 210, 14, 0, 13, 'The Valley of Fallen Heroes and Corp''rethar', 'West of Aldur''thar the Valley of Fallen Heroes and the broad Icecrown Glacier lie open to the sky. Scourge converters wake the valley''s dead, and banner-bearers fill the converted heroes with fearsome strength, while the gunships'' recon fighters and scouts fly overhead. The Ironwall Rampart dominates the fields below, held by the necromancer Grimkor the Wicked and his cult disciples. South of it, on the ground called the Conflagration, the Lich King''s elite form up before Corp''rethar, the Horror Gate and last barrier before the citadel: skeletal reavers that, it is feared, the Scourge can raise again whenever they fall, harbingers of horror on the battlements, and three crystal shards of horror, despair and suffering.', 'quests 13307, 13334 (Valley of Fallen Heroes and Icecrown Glacier west of Aldur''thar; converters and banner-bearers); quests 13312, 13337 (Ironwall Rampart overlooks the valley; Grimkor the Wicked and his Cult disciples); quests 13329, 13335 (the Conflagration before Corp''rethar; death knights and skeletal reavers that are reconstituted); quests 13316, 13338 (Corp''rethar the Horror Gate, last barrier; harbingers and guardians); quests 13328, 13339 (the three shards); quests 13313, 13314 (recon fighters and Orgrim''s Hammer scouts over the glacier)'),
(21015, 1, 210, 15, 0, 13, 'Blackwatch and the Fleshwerks', 'The Fleshwerks is the heart of the Scourge''s production of ghouls, abominations and flesh giants. Skeletal constructors labor night and day in its abomination and flesh giant labs, blood orbs and vats of embalming fluid keep the parts fresh, and finished abominations stand chained to the pillars, waiting to march. Its prize is Morbidus, a flesh giant champion, and in the Sanctum of Reanimation the ghoul mastermind Doctor Sabnok keeps his creation Patches in chains. From Blackwatch, on a ridge above, Darkrider Arly of the Ebon Blade and Crusader Olakin Sainrith of the Argent Crusade plan its destruction.', 'npc_text 13838 (Arly: the heart of ghoul, abomination and flesh giant production); quest 13106 description (Blackwatch on a ridge overlooking the Fleshwerks, west of Corp''rethar); quests 13117, 13119 (skeletal constructors summoned at altars in the east); quests 13134, 13144 (blood orbs, embalming fluid, chained abominations); quests 13152, 13235 (Sabnok and Patches in the Sanctum of Reanimation; Morbidus the flesh giant champion)'),
(21016, 1, 210, 16, 0, 13, 'Malykriss: The Vile Hold', 'Malykriss, the Vile Hold, lies east of Corp''rethar, nestled against Icecrown Citadel itself, and it is the seat of the Lich King''s metalworking. Skeletal runesmiths and saronite shapers work its forges and furnaces, lumbering atrocities and vargul brutes haul for them, iceskin sentries rest as stone along its walls, and lithe stalkers keep watch on the ramparts. In its yards a new generation of death knight initiates and adepts trains for the Lich King. Just to the west, on the Rise of Suffering within the Court of Bones, Vereth the Cunning of the Ebon Blade keeps a quiet watch on it all.', 'quest 13140 description (seat of the Lich King''s metalworking, east of Corp''rethar); quest 13138 description (nestled next to Icecrown Citadel; furnaces on the bottom level); quests 13143, 13146, 13147, 13160 (lithe stalkers on the ramparts; lumbering atrocities; umbral brutes are vargul; sleeping iceskin sentries); quest 13155 description (Rise of Suffering just west of Malykriss, inside the Court of Bones); zone_areas 4520: Death Knight Initiate, Death Knight Adept, Skeletal Runesmith, Saronite Shaper'),
(21017, 1, 210, 17, 0, 13, 'The Court of Bones and the Cathedral of Darkness', 'North of Icecrown Citadel spreads the Court of Bones, where cruel overseers drive reanimated miners at their work, skeletal archmagi and glacial bonelords stand among the bones, and webspinners and fallen spiderlords creep along its edges. Northwest of the citadel the Cult of the Damned keeps the Cathedral of Darkness, guarded by chosen zealots and glacial bonelords and served by cult acolytes. In the shadow of the Lich King''s walls, the dead outnumber everything else.', 'quest 13360 description (Court of Bones north of Icecrown Citadel); quest 13364 description (Cathedral of Darkness northwest of the citadel); zone_areas 4519, phase 1 spawns: Cruel Overseer, Reanimated Miner, Skeletal Archmage, Glacial Bonelord, Necrotic Webspinner, Fallen Spiderlord (the boneguard host there is phase 2 and phase 256 only); zone_areas 4521: Chosen Zealot, Cultist Acolyte, Glacial Bonelord'),
(21018, 1, 210, 18, 0, 13, 'Icecrown Citadel', 'Icecrown Citadel, the Lich King''s fortress, rises from the glacier crowned by the Frozen Throne. Citadel watchers guard its lower slopes, and below its walls an immense pit plunges several hundred feet into the ground, its purpose unknown but plainly of great importance to the Scourge. On the pit''s lip waits a death knight, Orbaz Bloodbane, and Knights of the Ebon Blade keep watch close by. Beneath the citadel lie the Frozen Halls, the way into its depths.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Icecrown_Citadel (the Frozen Throne at its summit); quests 13258, 13386 descriptions (an orifice leading several hundred feet into the ground; of high importance to the Scourge); quest 13164 description (under Icecrown Citadel an immense pit; Orbaz just outside its lip); zone_areas 4522: Hulking Horror, Citadel Watcher, Orbaz Bloodbane 31283, Ebon Blade Reaper 31316; mod-individual-progression IndividualProgressionPlayer.cpp (Icecrown Citadel and the Forge of Souls closed below state 16)'),
(21019, 1, 210, 19, 0, 15, 'The Argent Tournament Grounds', 'In the northeast of Icecrown, the Argent Crusade has raised the grounds of the Argent Tournament, where heroes of every banner test their skill against one another to ready themselves for the common enemy. Justicar Mariel Trueheart oversees it all as seneschal. Aspirants train against dummies on the northern grounds and face their first challenge in the Aspirants'' Ring, valiants meet Argent champions in the Argent Valiants'' Ring on the western edge, and champions ride against one another in the Ring of Champions near the stables. Argent Confessor Paletress keeps a small chapel of the Light, the Knights of the Ebon Blade camp on the north side, and the Crusaders'' Coliseum looms over the grounds.', 'quest 13667 description; creature_template 33817 subname Seneschal of the Argent Tournament; quests 13625, 13679, 13699, 13790 (training dummies on the northern grounds; Aspirants'' Ring; Argent Valiants'' Ring on the western edge; Ring of Champions near the stables); npc_text 14487 (Paletress: our little chapel of the Light); quest 13795 (the Ebon Blade''s camp on the north side); quest 14076 (the coliseum); mod-individual-progression checkIPPhasing: areas 4658, 4666, 4667, 4669-4674 phased from state 15; ipp_aware_npcs.sql ''-- Argent Tournament'''),
(21020, 1, 210, 20, 1, 15, 'The Silver Covenant Pavilion', 'The Silver Covenant Pavilion, the great Alliance tent in the northeastern part of the tournament grounds, houses the Alliance''s delegations. The high elves of the Silver Covenant speak for the Alliance at the tournament, and Arcanist Taelis enters newcomers in the rolls. Here the grand champions of Stormwind, Ironforge, Gnomeregan, Darnassus and the Exodar lead their cities'' delegations, with masters of arms and of mounts to train their riders, and just outside the tent the Alliance''s valiants hone their skills against one another in the Alliance Valiants'' Ring.', 'quest 13667 description (Taelis, the Silver Covenant''s representative, in the large Alliance tent in the northeast); creature_template subnames: Marshal Jacob Alerius, Lana Stouthammer, Ambrose Boltspark, Jaelyne Evensong, Colosos (Grand Champions); masters of arms and of horses, rams, mechanostriders, nightsabers, elekks; quest 13665 (the Alliance Valiants'' Ring just outside our tent); zone_icecrown.cpp npc_guardian_pavilion (Trespasser! 63986/63987 teleport the other faction out of 4676/4677); WMOAreaTable: 4667 and 4677 are groups of the pavilion model 5569; zone_icecrown.cpp npc_guardian_pavilion acts only when the guardian stands in 4676/4677; quest 13667 (Alliance only, turned in to Arcanist Taelis 33625 inside the tent)'),
(21021, 1, 210, 21, 2, 15, 'The Sunreaver Pavilion', 'The Sunreaver Pavilion, the great Horde tent in the southeastern part of the tournament grounds, houses the Horde''s delegations. The blood elf magi of the Sunreavers speak for the Horde at the tournament, and Magister Edien Sunhollow enters newcomers in the rolls. Here the grand champions of Orgrimmar, Sen''jin, Thunder Bluff, the Undercity and Silvermoon lead their cities'' delegations, with masters of arms and of mounts to train their riders, and just outside the tent the Horde''s valiants spar with one another in the Horde Valiants'' Ring.', 'quest 13668 description (Edien Sunhollow, the Sunreaver representative, in the large Horde tent in the southeast); creature_template subnames: Mokra the Skullcrusher, Zul''tore, Runok Wildmane, Deathstalker Visceri, Eressea Dawnsinger (Grand Champions); masters of arms, wolves, raptors, kodos, horses, hawkstriders; areas.json 4673 The Horde Valiants'' Ring beside the Horde tent (Horde valiant spawns there); zone_icecrown.cpp npc_guardian_pavilion (Trespasser! teleports the other faction out of 4676/4677); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Sunreavers (blood elf magi of Dalaran); WMOAreaTable: 4666 and 4676 are groups of the pavilion model 5569; quest 13668 (Horde only, turned in to Magister Edien Sunhollow 33542 inside the tent)'),
(21022, 1, 210, 22, 0, 13, 'Deathspeaker''s Watch', 'Deathspeaker''s Watch is a Cult of the Damned encampment on a rise in the northeast of Icecrown. Dark zealots and ritualists keep captives in black cages there, and some of their prisoners already lie sacrificed. The ruthless Deathspeaker Kharos commands the camp and has his men fortify it, and from an altar overlooking it all the infamous Doctor Kohler practices his arts.', 'quest 14017 description (the infamous Doctor Kohler; an altar overlooking the cultist camp); quest 14105 description (the ruthless Deathspeaker Kharos has his men fortifying their positions; Hrothgar''s Landing quest, not used as a trigger); zone_areas 4743: Dark Zealot, Dark Ritualist, Captive Aspirant, Sacrificed Aspirant, Black Cage, Deathspeaker Kharos 34808, Doctor Kohler 35113'),
(21030, 2, 210, 1, 0, 13, 'The Lich King', 'The Lich King rules the Scourge from the Frozen Throne atop Icecrown Citadel. He was once Arthas Menethil, prince of Lordaeron, who took up the runeblade Frostmourne in Northrend, turned on his own people and at last joined with the Lich King Ner''zhul upon the throne. Those who fight him in Icecrown say he strikes recklessly, without care or caution, and one death knight sneers that the boy is not used to losing. His land is his fortress, and through his servants he watches much of what moves within it.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Arthas_Menethil (Frostmourne; merged with Ner''zhul on the Frozen Throne; Warcraft III and The Frozen Throne only); quest 13045 reward text (Arthas strikes recklessly, without care or caution); quest 13174 reward text (that boy is not used to losing); quest 12887 reward text (he can still see through his Scourge minions)'),
(21031, 2, 210, 2, 0, 13, 'Highlord Darion Mograine', 'Highlord Darion Mograine is the master of the Knights of the Ebon Blade, the death knights who broke from the Lich King at Light''s Hope Chapel when Tirion Fordring helped Mograine free them from his hold; Acherus, the Ebon Hold, is now the order''s home. In Icecrown the order wages its own war of vengeance. Its knights hold Death''s Rise and the Shadow Vault, keep watch on the Scourge from camps across the glacier and lend their counsel to the gunships, and Mograine himself moves among them.', 'npc_text 13526, 13527 (Arete''s tale: at Light''s Hope Tirion helped Mograine break the Lich King''s hold; Ebon Hold taken); quest 13164 description (Mograine found where Orbaz is hiding); quest 13105 reward text (Koltira aids the Horde on Orgrim''s Hammer, Thassarian the Alliance on the Skybreaker); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Darion_Mograine (Wrath of the Lich King)'),
(21032, 2, 210, 3, 0, 13, 'Grand Admiral Westwind', 'Barean Westwind, admiral of the Scarlet Fleet, is the master of the Scarlet Onslaught. By Lord-Commander Arete''s account he presented himself unlooked for to High General Abbendis at New Hearthglen, undermined her and took the reins of command, and once she was dead he made a mysterious exit. Arete suspects he is somewhere on the Onslaught''s island off Icecrown''s coast, though none of the spies who came back could place him.', 'npc_text 13528 (Arete: Westwind presented himself to Abbendis at New Hearthglen, undermined her, took the reins of command; after her death a mysterious exit); npc_text 13529 (suspects he is down there; spies could not place him); creature_template 29621 subname Leader of the Scarlet Onslaught; 27951 Grand Admiral of the Scarlet Fleet'),
(21033, 2, 210, 4, 0, 13, 'Lady Nightswood', 'Lady Nightswood is a banshee. Once she had a home in the lush woods of Quel''Thalas, a husband and children, until the Lich King took it all away in the blink of an eye. She served him at the Shadow Vault until the Knights of the Ebon Blade broke his hold on her, and now she has gone into Jotunheim and taken possession of the vrykul''s bone witch at Njorndar Village. She cannot strike at the Lich King directly, but from within the witch she means to pay him back threefold.', 'npc_text 13715 (the Bone Witch: Quel''Thalas, husband, children; pay him back threefold); quest 12893 description (Vile, Nightswood and the Leaper broken from his will); quest 12999 description (she possessed the bone witch of Njorndar)'),
(21034, 2, 210, 5, 0, 13, 'Crusader Bridenbrad', 'Crusader Bridenbrad is the hero of the Broken Front. When the Scourge came down upon the allied force there and its men scattered, he alone came back, dragging more than a dozen soldiers to safety one by one through the carnage. He has not come back since. He was last seen heading for the Silent Vigil in the far northeast of Icecrown, and Tirion Fordring wants him found so that he can be honored for his valor.', 'quest 13068 description'),
(21035, 2, 210, 6, 0, 13, 'Crusader Olakin Sainrith', 'Crusader Olakin Sainrith is the Argent Crusade''s contribution to the Ebon Blade''s war on the Fleshwerks, sent to Blackwatch to stand beside Darkrider Arly. To him the dead are heroes who fell in defense of the living, and they must never be left to the Scourge''s grisly work or raised against those who still live. He burns the corpses of the Scourge''s victims with his own torch rather than leave them to it, and he studies every new horror the Fleshwerks turns out.', 'quest 13106 reward text (Olakin here is the Argent Crusade''s contribution); quest 13211 description and reward text; quests 13136, 13138, 13140 (the shards and the plates)'),
(21036, 2, 210, 7, 0, 13, 'Matthias Lehner', 'Matthias Lehner is a boy, or the ghost of one, who speaks out of the dark of Naz''anak, the Forgotten Depths, beneath Icecrown Citadel. He says he saw ''him'' throw something all the way down there, saying he would not need it anymore and that it made him weak. Whoever touches it, the boy warns, will make ''him'' angry, and ''he'' will come looking for them unless they hide. Matthias is plainly afraid of him.', 'quests 13271, 13390 reward text (I saw him get rid of it... said it made him weak); creature_text 31237 group 0 (You shouldn''t have done that! He''s not going to like it.); quests 13275, 13391 descriptions (he''s going to come looking for you, unless you hide)'),
(21037, 2, 210, 8, 0, 15, 'Justicar Mariel Trueheart', 'Justicar Mariel Trueheart is the seneschal of the Argent Tournament, who welcomes every newcomer on behalf of the Argent Crusade. Many have been the divisions among those who oppose the Scourge, she reminds them, but the time has come for heroes of every banner to test their blades against one another before they face their mutual enemy. She sends Alliance newcomers to the Silver Covenant''s Arcanist Taelis and those of the Horde to the Sunreavers'' Magister Edien Sunhollow to be entered in the rolls.', 'creature_template 33817 subname Seneschal of the Argent Tournament; npc_text 14425 (On behalf of the Argent Crusade, I welcome you); quests 13667, 13668 descriptions'),
(21040, 3, 210, 1, 0, 13, 'The Argent Crusade''s March', 'The Argent Crusade has fought across continents, even worlds, to reach Icecrown, and here it faces its greatest challenge: the destruction of the Lich King and his Scourge. It fights divided from the Alliance and the Horde, who are at war with each other and lend it no support, and its envoys call on every volunteer to join the cause, for divided all will fall. Where both factions failed, the Crusade broke into Icecrown, but its breach was rebuffed at once and with force. The Lich King''s answer was swift and brutal, and Highlord Tirion Fordring''s Argent Vanguard now stands on the defensive.', 'quest 13036 description and reward text; quests 13226, 13227 descriptions (divided we shall all fall; the Crusade accepts all volunteers)'),
(21041, 3, 210, 2, 0, 13, 'The War on Jotunheim', 'Duke Lankral, now master of the Shadow Vault, has turned the Ebon Blade against the vrykul of Jotunheim, over the mountains to the west. Every contest of ascension there sends its winner to Ymirheim and leaves its loser a vargul, and Lankral means to see far more vargul than Ymirjar come out of them. His knights humiliate Jotunheim''s warriors on their own sparring ledge, burn its banners, plant Ebon Blade standards beside its dead, set its buildings ablaze from stolen proto-drakes and shoot its riders from the sky, day after day.', 'quest 12938 description and reward text; quest 12943 reward text (a foe that dwarfs us; we must outthink them); quests 12939, 12995, 13084, 13071, 13069 (challenges, banners, burning, proto-drakes)'),
(21042, 3, 210, 3, 0, 13, 'The Host of Suffering', 'At the Shadow Vault, Keritose Bloodblade has found that the Cult of the Damned, fleeing the Ebon Blade''s slaughter, left eyes of dominion behind: tools that let any mind of some power command a lesser undead precisely. He has a use for them. The saronite quarry down the path to the southwest pulls immense amounts of ore from the ground, and Keritose wants to know what the Scourge is building with it. He begins by sending stolen undead in among its hounds, lookouts and crystals to weaken it from within before his gryphon riders strike.', 'quest 13168 description and reward text (eyes of dominion; the Cult''s retreat); quests 13169, 13170, 13171, 13172 descriptions'),
(21043, 3, 210, 4, 1, 13, 'The Skybreaker''s Campaign', 'After its assault on the glacier from the ground came to grief, the Alliance carries its war in Icecrown aboard the Skybreaker, which it calls one of the most advanced works of engineering in Azeroth. From its decks High Captain Justin Bartlett lays the groundwork for the assault on Arthas, Chief Engineer Boltwrench keeps the ship in the air, and Absalan the Pious speaks for the Argent Crusade, whose help the Alliance knows it will need. The death knight Thassarian serves aboard as well, an advisor who knows the enemy from the inside.', 'quest 13418 description and reward text (failure on the ground; the Skybreaker; groundwork; Absalan; the Crusade''s help); quest 13290 description (Boltwrench keeps them from being sprinkled across the glacier); quest 13286 reward text (a former servant of the Lich King); creature 29799 Thassarian, 30344 Bartlett, 30345 Boltwrench on map 623 (the Skybreaker transport)'),
(21044, 3, 210, 5, 2, 13, 'Orgrim''s Hammer''s Campaign', 'Orgrim''s Hammer, the Horde''s gunship, flies out of the Scourge''s reach high over the ground between Mord''rethar and Aldur''thar. The Alliance rushed into Icecrown unprepared, its officers say, while the Horde took its time and made ready. Sky-Reaver Korm Blackscar commands from the deck and swears vengeance on the Scourge and the Alliance alike, the goblin Chief Engineer Copperclaw crows over his inventions below, and Brother Keltan speaks for the Argent Crusade. The death knight Koltira Deathweaver serves aboard as an advisor who knows the enemy from the inside.', 'quest 13224 description (overhead between Mord''rethar and Aldur''thar; out of reach of the Scourge) and reward text (damn the Scourge and damn the Alliance); quest 13419 description and reward text; quest 13238 description (Copperclaw, goblins); quest 13260 description (our resident death knight); creature 29795 Koltira, 30824 Korm, 30825 Copperclaw on map 622 (Orgrim''s Hammer transport)'),
(21045, 3, 210, 6, 0, 13, 'The Heart of the Lich King', 'Below Icecrown Citadel lies a weakness in the Lich King''s defenses, an opening in more ways than one, and the gunship''s death knight adviser means to exploit it. The site is a pit that plunges deep into the ground beneath the citadel''s walls, and hulking horrors stand guard over it. A small force has already been sent there with a stack of potent saronite bombs, made by the Scourge and taken from them, to secure the site and blow it open. Done right, a single blast could deal the Lich King''s forces a heavy blow at the very foot of his fortress.', 'quest 13258 description (Koltira: schematics, an orifice several hundred feet into the ground); quest 13386 description (Thassarian: an opening, a structural weakness, men sent with borrowed saronite bombs); quests 13259, 13387 (Hulking Horrors guarding the site; Scourge-made bombs)'),
(21046, 3, 210, 7, 0, 15, 'The Argent Tournament', 'The Argent Crusade has called heroes of every banner to its tournament in northeastern Icecrown, so that the Alliance and the Horde may test their skill and valor against one another before they face the Scourge together. Each newcomer is entered in the rolls as an aspirant, by the Silver Covenant or by the Sunreavers, and learns to fight from the saddle with lance and shield against the training dummies on the northern grounds. Once proven, aspirants may ride on behalf of their capital cities, rising through the ranks of valiant and champion toward the grand melee.', 'quests 13667, 13668 descriptions and reward text; quests 13625, 13828 (lance, mounts, training dummies)'),
(21047, 3, 210, 8, 0, 15, 'The Black Knight', 'A rider called the Black Knight has made a name for himself in the tournament''s lists, and every combatant scheduled to face him has met an untimely end. His story of his own origins has proven a sham. Crusader Rhydalla of the Argent Crusade now means to prove that the deaths were murder and to tie them to him before he strikes again, and she knows a way to reveal how the dead truly died: a seer''s crystal from the unbound seers of Crystalsong Forest, imbued with the power of the Light to cut through lies and deceit.', 'quest 13641 description and reward text; creature_text 33417 groups 0-1 (Rhydalla imbues the crystal); westfall.json 4011 and silverpine.json 13006 (the claimed origins, told there)');
INSERT INTO `mod_lore_codex_part` (`Entry`, `Part`, `MinState`, `MaxState`, `Body`, `Sources`) VALUES
(21000, 1, 15, 255, 'In the northeast of Icecrown, the Argent Crusade has raised the grounds of a great tournament beside a new coliseum. Heroes of the Alliance and the Horde, and knights of the Ebon Blade, come to test their skill against one another, so that the strongest will be ready when the time comes to face their common enemy.', 'quest 13667 description (heroes of all banners test their blades against one another in preparation for the mutual enemy); quest 14076 description (the coliseum is complete); quest 13795 (the Ebon Blade delegation)'),
(21001, 1, 0, 255, 'The chill of death stirred in the west, and the Lich King answered the Crusade''s breach with an assault on the Vanguard itself. Siegemaster Fezzik readied the camp''s defenses at the front gate: atop each of its four towers stood a retractable cannon, blessed by Father Gustav, and Argent champions took the field in the valley below.', 'quest 13070 description and reward text; quest 13086 description (four towers, retractable cannons blessed by Gustav); spell_area 57569 (Chapter II, phase 64) in 4501/4504 from DONE 13070; phase 64 spawns Argent Cannon 30236, Argent Champion 30188'),
(21001, 2, 0, 255, 'The assault broke against the Vanguard''s walls. From the towers the cannons shattered the Scourge and brought down the frost wyrms sent against the walls, while Tirion fought on the field himself. The valley was won back and the web walls blocking the Breach torn down, and the Crusade pitched a camp outside the Breach for the push into Scourgeholme.', 'quest 13086 description and reward text; quest 13104 description (valley reclaimed, web walls down, tent outside the Breach); spell_area 57674 (Chapter III, phase 128) from DONE 13086; phase 128 spawns in 4504: Ebon Watcher 30596, Father Gustav 30683, Silas 30686, Spitzpatrick 30714'),
(21001, 3, 0, 255, 'With Crusaders'' Pinnacle taken, Tirion and his officers have moved on into Icecrown and the camp outside the Breach has been struck. The Vanguard remains the Crusade''s rear camp: its infirmary still full of wounded, its quartermaster, smiths and flight master serving those bound for the front, and Arch Druid Lilliandra offering what help she can.', 'quest 13157 description (Tirion and the survivors at Crusaders'' Pinnacle); spell_area: no Vanguard phase after DONE 13157; phase 1 spawns (phaseMask 131): Injured Crusader 30242, Aliocha Segard (quartermaster), Halig Fireforge, Aedan Moran (flight master), Lilliandra 30630; npc_text 13844 (Lilliandra)'),
(21002, 1, 0, 255, 'When the Lich King''s assault on the Vanguard failed, Scourgeholme turned to slash and burn: the crusaders it held captive were to be executed and raised in his service, and reanimated crusaders now walk its tiers where the prisoners once lay.', 'quest 13118 description (slash and burn; prisoners executed and raised); spell_area 57674 (Chapter III, phase 128) in 4505/4506 from DONE 13086: Captured Crusaders 30407 (phase 2) gone, Reanimated Crusader 30202 x36 in their place'),
(21002, 2, 0, 255, 'The lords of Scourgeholme have fallen: Salranax, Yath''amon and Talonox were cut down in their halls. The Ebon Watcher knows they will be replaced, but for a day at least, he says, the air about Scourgeholme stands still.', 'quest 13125 description and reward text'),
(21002, 3, 0, 255, 'Crusade Architect Silas sees more than a rancid pit here. Tirion has already named the fortress he means to raise from this ground Justice Keep, and Silas sends to Crystalsong Forest for its first stones: heartwood from the Unbound Thicket and elven masonry from the Ruins of Shandaral, which by their nature repel disease, rot and plague.', 'quest 13130 description and reward text'),
(21003, 1, 0, 255, 'The Crusade took the pinnacle back. Crusader Lord Dalfors and his priests burned what the Scourge had made of their dead, and a blessed banner of the Crusade, planted atop the skulls, sanctified the ground while the Scourge threw wave after wave against it. The Lich King''s voice rang over the field, driving his creations on, and still the pinnacle held.', 'quest 13141 description and reward text; creature_text 31003 groups 0-3 (Dalfors); creature_text 31013 groups 0-3 (the Lich King, phase 128 only); zone_icecrown.cpp Battle for Crusaders'' Pinnacle (banner, priests, masons, NPC_LK 31013)'),
(21003, 2, 0, 255, 'Crusaders'' Pinnacle is now the Argent Crusade''s stronghold inside Icecrown, where Tirion Fordring plans the long road to the citadel''s gates. Masons raise its walls, and here lie soldiers the Crusade carried off the Broken Front, among them a Horde warlord and an Alliance marshal, each asking that word of his death be taken to his gunship.', 'quest 13157 description and reward text; npc_text 13896 (Tirion: only the first step); creature 32320 Argent Mason in 4580; quests 13224, 13225 descriptions (Hork Strongbrow and Ivalius, pulled from the Broken Front, dying)'),
(21005, 1, 0, 255, 'The Shadow Vault has fallen to the Knights of the Ebon Blade. The Ocular was destroyed to blind the Lich King. Baron Sliver, who had only feigned loyalty, broke Vile, Nightswood and the Leaper from his will with a sovereign rod, and General Lightsbane fell beside his own forge. Duke Lankral commands the vault now, and its knights fight tooth and nail to hold it against the Scourge.', 'quests 12887-12899 descriptions and reward text; quest 12938 description and reward text (Lankral in charge; barely holding); creature_text 29851, 29858 (Lightsbane, Nightswood at the forge)'),
(21007, 1, 0, 255, 'Bethod Feigr was Thane Ufrang''s champion until his fight for ascendance in Valhalas, when Thane Illskar sabotaged him with dark magic and he lost, to be reduced to a vargul. His prayers to the Lady of the Sword were answered: a challenger threw down his sword before Illskar in the Circle of Suffering, and the thane died for his treachery.', 'quest 13059 description and reward text; creature_text 30475 (Illskar accepts the challenge of Bethod''s sword)'),
(21008, 1, 0, 255, 'Geirrvif has opened Valhalas to outsiders who have made a name for themselves. The vrykul who fell to them do not concern her: a warrior who can be bested is unworthy and fit only to be a lowly vargul. Valhalas, she says, is a place for combat of every kind against many kinds of foes, and she means to learn whether the newcomers are truly worthy.', 'quest 13213 reward text'),
(21008, 2, 0, 255, 'Word of one challenger''s victories reached deep into Icecrown Citadel, and Prince Sandoval, a blood prince, came to Valhalas in person to end the matter. He fell in the pit. Gjonner, who held it an honor merely to kneel at the prince''s feet, was sickened, and Geirrvif now greets the victor as a champion.', 'quest 13219 description and reward text; npc_text 13946 (Champion, it is good to see you again)'),
(21010, 1, 0, 255, 'The captives in the Saronite Mines are the Argent Crusade''s own people, mining saronite for the Lich King day and night, and the Crusade''s envoy aboard the gunship has promised Tirion Fordring to bring them out alive. Those freed so far come back half mad, complaining of voices in their heads.', 'quests 13300, 13302 descriptions and reward text; creature_template 31397 Saronite Mine Slave faction 2070 (Argent Crusade)'),
(21010, 2, 0, 255, 'Deep in the mines the Ymirjar keep something else in chains: Darkspeaker R''khem, a creature that rose from below to see what the noise was and was captured. It speaks directly into the minds of those who come near, painful and strange, and promises a rich reward to whoever brings it the foreman''s key, all the while pushing at their thoughts as if to make sure the key is handed over willingly.', 'quest 13308 description, request and reward text (thoughts painful and strange; reward first, then you will willingly hand me the key)'),
(21011, 1, 0, 255, 'The Broken Front was an Alliance assault on the gate, and it was broken when Horde soldiers fell upon it as well. Neither side has forgotten it, and the hatred born on this field now rides the gunships above Icecrown as surely as their war on the Scourge.', 'quest 13228 description and reward text (Horde); quest 13231 description and reward text (Alliance); quests 13233, 13234 (each side hunts the other in Icecrown)'),
(21012, 1, 0, 255, 'The cultists of Aldur''thar stumbled upon something that could threaten every plan against the citadel. Their sect''s leader, Alumeth, sacrificed himself in a ritual, and his followers channel power into his soul to make him a mighty adversary, Alumeth the Ascended. He has been struck down, but his spirit lingers.', 'quests 13346, 13367 descriptions and reward text'),
(21012, 2, 0, 255, 'Hidden in the sky above the gate are two airports no one is meant to see. Goblin engineers of the Horde found a new energy they call infra-green and used it to hide themselves close enough to bomb the Scourge, and the Alliance, which copied the trick, keeps a cloaked airport of its own nearby. Each side warns its pilots away from the other''s dome.', 'quest 13379 description (Tezzla hides near the Scourge, near enough to bomb them; the Alliance stole the technology; avoid their dome); quest 13383 description (the goblins found infra-green; hidden Alliance airport; avoid the Horde airport); zone_areas 4510: Cloak Dome gameobjects, Kibli Killohertz 32444, Fringe Engineer Tezzla 32430'),
(21015, 1, 0, 255, 'The jagged metal shards found in every ghoul of the Fleshwerks were cut from runed saronite plates forged by the skeletal runesmiths of Malykriss. The Scourge, Olakin judged, is desperate enough to make a weapon of anything, and these shards could pierce armor with enough force.', 'quest 13136 (shards in every ghoul); quest 13140 description and reward text (plates match the shards; desperate enough to make a weapon of anything); quest 13138 description (these could pierce armor)'),
(21015, 2, 0, 255, 'With the altars broken and the labs in ruins, the Shadow Vault sent Margrave Dhakar and his knights to bring down Morbidus, and the Lich King''s prized flesh giant fell at the western end of the Fleshwerks. Arly means the Lich King to know from it that the rest of his forces are vulnerable too.', 'quest 13235 description and reward text'),
(21017, 1, 15, 255, 'For a time, crusaders from the Argent Tournament kept a forward camp on the southern side of Corp''rethar, and champions rode out from it on campaign chargers, trampling boneguard footmen under their horses'' hooves and striking down the Lich King''s lieutenants and commanders in the Court of Bones.', 'quests 13847-13864 descriptions (forward camp on the southern side of Corp''rethar; campaign charger; footmen trampled); spell_area 64576 (phase 256) in 4519 and 4522 only while those quests are in the log; phase 256 spawns Crusader Maran 34180, Stabled Campaign Warhorse 34125, Argent Peacekeeper 34179'),
(21018, 1, 0, 255, 'At the bottom of the pit lies Naz''anak, the Forgotten Depths, a cavern of dark water and ice where faceless ones lurk. A blast at the pit''s lip sent the first visitor in a long while tumbling down into it, and beneath its water lies something pulsing, sealed in ice.', 'quests 13263, 13389 (the bombs, the fall into the pit, the pulsing object beneath the water); zone_areas 4522: Faceless Lurker 31691'),
(21018, 2, 16, 255, 'The Frozen Halls now stand open, and with them the way into the citadel itself. Argent crusaders and Knights of the Ebon Blade keep watch side by side at the approaches, and the assault on the Lich King''s fortress has begun.', 'creatures 38493 Argent Crusader and 38505 Knight of the Ebon Blade at the Frozen Halls (z 636); mod-individual-progression: the Frozen Halls and Icecrown Citadel from state 16'),
(21022, 1, 15, 255, 'The captives in the cages are aspirants of the Argent Tournament, whose grounds lie just to the east, and the dead are aspirants too. The cult has camped close enough to strike at the tournament whenever it chooses, and the tournament in turn sends its champions out to thin the cultists here.', 'zone_areas 4743: Captive Aspirant 34716, Sacrificed Aspirant 35097; quest 14017 description (the rise west of the tournament grounds); quest 13791 description (the cult''s strong presence around Deathspeaker''s Watch); mod-individual-progression: the tournament from state 15'),
(21030, 1, 0, 255, 'When the Argent Crusade fought for Crusaders'' Pinnacle, the Lich King''s voice rang across the field, urging his creations to feast on the flesh of the living and calling on the crusaders to lay down their arms and surrender their souls. They did not, and the pinnacle was lost to him.', 'creature_text 31013 groups 0-3; quest 13141 reward text'),
(21030, 2, 0, 255, 'At Balargarde Fortress he appeared before a challenge to Overthane Balargarde, saw through the banshee Lady Nightswood''s disguise and ordered the overthane to finish his foes. When Balargarde fell instead, he only told the victors that their efforts were for naught, for the frozen heart of Icecrown awaits.', 'creature_text 31083 groups 0-6 and 31016 groups 5-7'),
(21030, 3, 0, 255, 'In the Cathedral of Darkness he met Tirion Fordring again, mocking him that this time they did not stand on holy ground and that a paladin would never destroy humanity''s only chance to redeem its most wayward son. Tirion struck at his heart with the Ashbringer all the same, and the Lich King fell to his knees, swearing that the old man would pay.', 'creature_text 32184 groups 0-6; creature_text 32239 groups 5-8 (Tirion); zone_icecrown.cpp Tirion''s Gambit (the Lich King kneels after the strike)'),
(21031, 1, 0, 255, 'The Ebon Watcher who advised the Argent Crusade outside the Breach was Mograine himself. He served Tirion only to pay a debt, he told his knights, since the Highlord had freed them; once the Crusade had its foothold inside Icecrown, the Ebon Blade would part ways with it, for a different destiny awaits the order.', 'quest 13105 reward text (Highlord Darion Mograine peers at you); npc_text 13856, 13857 (the Ebon Watcher: payment of a debt; a different destiny awaits)'),
(21031, 2, 0, 255, 'He tracked Orbaz Bloodbane, the self-proclaimed hand of the Lich King, to the pit beneath the citadel and came in person to see him die. Orbaz, he said, would never have what it takes to lead anything, not even a legion of mindless skeletons. His only epitaph for the traitor was a curt ''Good riddance.''', 'creature_text 31290 groups 0-3; creature_text 31283 group 6 (There you are Darion!); quest 13164 reward text'),
(21031, 3, 0, 255, 'When Tirion''s gamble in the Cathedral of Darkness left him struck down among the Lich King''s zealots, Mograine came with Thassarian, Koltira and his knights, broke up the cult''s gathering and saw the survivors out through a portal. He would not stay to finish the wounded king: their chance would come, he said, and for once it was Tirion who stood in their debt.', 'creature_text 32312 groups 0-1, 32310, 32311; zone_icecrown.cpp Tirion''s Gambit (summons 32309-32312)'),
(21032, 1, 0, 255, 'A note in the grand admiral''s own hand, taken from the Onslaught''s baggage, settled it: he is on the island, keeping himself secluded for now. He writes of a glorious day soon to come, when the Scarlet Onslaught will wash over first the Lich King and then the rest of the world, and bring order to Azeroth at last.', 'quest 12839 description; quest 12838 (intel from the Onslaught''s baggage trunks)'),
(21032, 2, 0, 255, 'His captains knew only that the Onslaught had raised Archbishop Landgren from death and set him over the Crimson Cathedral. Landgren was slain again, and Lord-Commander Arete, stepping through a gate to question his soul, threatened to destroy it until it gave up the secret: the grand admiral hides in a cave at the island''s south end, the Hidden Hollow, preparing for the final battle against the Lich King.', 'quest 12840 reward text; quest 12847 description and reward text; creature_text 29560 groups 1-5 and 29572 groups 0-4'),
(21032, 3, 0, 255, 'Found in the Hidden Hollow, Westwind raised the sphere of magic that had saved him at New Hearthglen, and it was stripped away. Then he shed his weak little shell: the grand admiral was the dreadlord Mal''Ganis. Beaten, he fled to gather his strength on his homeworld, swearing revenge on the Lich King and on his foes alike. The Scarlets, Arete laughed, had been taken in by demons yet again.', 'quest 12852 description and reward text; creature_text 29621 groups 0-6'),
(21033, 1, 0, 255, 'Her first blow fell in the Underhalls, where Dr. Terrible worked on what he called the ultimate weapon, flesh giants like his prototype Nergeld. The doctor was drawn out and slain by his own creation. A fine poke in the eye for the Lich King, she said, but she meant to do better.', 'quests 13042, 13043 descriptions and reward text; creature_text 30404 (Dr. Terrible)'),
(21033, 2, 0, 255, 'Through the Eye of the Lich King in Kul''galar Keep she learned that the val''kyr Vardmadra was coming to judge Iskalder, said to be the finest vrykul warrior who ever lived. Iskalder was taken from his slumber, and when Vardmadra came to Battlescar Spire to witness his battle, Nightswood seized her: this, she told the val''kyr, was the start of her final revenge.', 'quests 13121, 13133, 13137 descriptions and reward text; creature_text 30945 groups 0-4 (Vardmadra), 30955 group 0 (Nightswood)'),
(21033, 3, 0, 255, 'Wearing Vardmadra, she sat in judgment over a challenge to Overthane Balargarde, master of Jotunheim, and he fell, though the Lich King himself came and saw through her. Her revenge, she says, is complete. She will remain in the bone witch until the vrykul are no longer a threat, wishing only that she could be there when the Lich King is finally brought down.', 'quest 13142 description and reward text; creature_text 31016 groups 2-3 (Balargarde greets Vardmadra), 31083 group 2'),
(21034, 1, 0, 255, 'He was found at the Silent Vigil beside his fire, carrying the plague of undeath. He warned his finder off, wanting no one else exposed, and confessed his only fear: not death, but serving the traitor Arthas after it. Tirion would not leave such a man to that fate and set out to find him salvation.', 'quest 13072 description and reward text'),
(21034, 2, 0, 255, 'Keeper Remulos sent an emerald acorn, and it refreshed and renewed him, buying precious hours, though the plague still gripped him. Alexstrasza the Life-Binder gave her breath, warning that she could not promise to strip the plague without harming the body; the cleansing burned away some of the corruption, but not all. Bridenbrad''s hope was renewed all the same, and he said he could depart without fear.', 'quests 13075, 13076 descriptions and reward text; quests 13077, 13079, 13080 descriptions and reward text'),
(21034, 3, 0, 255, 'At the last, Tirion turned to the naaru A''dal, who promised that the Light would take care of its own and that Bridenbrad would not endure the corruption of undeath. The crusader was pale and failing when the blessing reached him, and as he spoke his last words of hope for the land a gentle ringing filled the air, and he died with a smile.', 'quests 13081, 13082 descriptions and reward text; smart_scripts 30562 (on 13082: summon A''dal, the Spirit of Bridenbrad)'),
(21034, 4, 0, 255, 'His tabard was found in a chest at the Silent Vigil and carried back to Crusaders'' Pinnacle. Tirion had already felt a small bit of light leave the land. With A''dal''s blessing, he said, Bridenbrad would know no evil in his afterlife, and the Crusade would take heart in his shining example.', 'quest 13083 description, completion and reward text'),
(21035, 1, 0, 255, 'The Scourge carried Olakin off, and Arly, to whom one crusader is much like another, sent for him only because the argents would not see it so. His body was recovered in pieces from the corpulent horrors of the Fleshwerks and stitched together on the slab in the Sanctum of Reanimation. He stands again, and Arly means him to remember that no one is rescued from the Scourge twice.', 'quest 13212 description and reward text; quest 13220 description and reward text; spell_area 58139 (Fleshwerks Phase, phase 64) in 4588 from DONE 13144 until 13220 complete; creature 30708 phaseMask 1, Darkrider Arly 30631 phaseMask 65'),
(21036, 1, 0, 255, 'At an old army encampment north of the Valley of Lost Hope he showed how the prince raised an army of the dead. Making armies out of corpses was easy, the boy said. The prince''s true power was killing his own men, with whom he had shared many battles, because it had to be done.', 'quests 13305, 13394 (the old army encampment); quests 13236, 13395 description and reward text; creature 31254 Lordaeron Footsoldier, 32414 Lordaeron Captain, phaseMask 2, in 4622'),
(21036, 2, 0, 255, 'At Sindragosa''s Fall he showed how a whole brood of blue dragons that fell there is being raised one by one by his servants, and how the greatest of them was raised by the Lich King himself, who called on Sindragosa to rise and lead the Frostbrood to war. Even the mighty wyrms had to heed his call, Matthias said, so how could a mere mortal resist him?', 'quests 13359, 13398 description and reward text; smart_scripts 32423 (summons 32443 on 13359/13398 complete); creature_text 32443 group 0'),
(21036, 3, 0, 255, 'In the Court of Bones he showed the one battle in which the prince came close to dying, a duel with Illidan Stormrage. Afterward, Matthias said, the prince understood that what held him back was that he was still human: he could feel, he could bleed, he still had a heart. The first thing he did as king was rid himself of it.', 'quests 13361, 13400 description and reward text; creature_template 32326 Prince Arthas Menethil, 32587/32588 Illidan Stormrage (the Prince''s Destiny vision)'),
(21037, 1, 0, 255, 'Those who rise through every challenge she formally enters in the champions'' grand melee, where they may compete for the grand championship of the tournament. Every champion, she holds, must have a squire, and she appoints one of the Crusade''s own to ride with each, proudly bearing the banner of every city that has named that hero its champion.', 'quest 13702 reward text (and the matching 13732-13740)'),
(21040, 1, 0, 255, 'Bronze proto-drakes of Penumbrius''s brood carried rescuers across the Breach to pull captured crusaders out of Scourgeholme. Arthas strikes recklessly, Tirion judged, without care or caution, and the Crusade had caught him off guard; it would bolster its defenses and weather the storm to come.', 'quests 13044, 13045 descriptions and reward text'),
(21040, 2, 0, 255, 'The storm came out of the west, and the Vanguard held. Its blessed cannons broke the Scourge and its frost wyrms while Tirion fought on the field below. The valley was won back and the web walls torn down, and Tirion turned to the death knight called the Ebon Watcher, whose intimate knowledge of the Scourge would serve the push through the Breach.', 'quest 13086 description and reward text; quests 13104, 13105 descriptions; 13104 reward text (served under the Lich King before Light''s Hope)'),
(21040, 3, 0, 255, 'With the Ebon Blade''s help Scourgeholme''s lords were struck down and its numbers thinned, and the Crusade carried a blessed banner to Crusaders'' Pinnacle and sanctified the ground. The Argent Crusade stands inside the walls of Icecrown now, in open defiance of the Lich King, though Tirion knows that a long and arduous road to the gates of the citadel still lies ahead.', 'quests 13125, 13139, 13141, 13157 descriptions and reward text'),
(21041, 1, 0, 255, 'Lankral''s decree was read aloud in the hall of Thane Ufrang the Mighty, a patient strategist who liked to bide his time. Ufrang''s answer was to attack the messenger, and he died for it. Against a foe that dwarfs his knights in stature and in numbers, Lankral says, the Ebon Blade must outthink the vrykul, and with Ufrang gone it has an advantage to press.', 'quest 12943 description and reward text; creature_text 29919 groups 1-4'),
(21041, 2, 0, 255, 'Not every blow landed. Vaelen the Flayed walked into a vrykul trap and was taken in chains with his whole contingent of death knights, a loss the vault could ill afford with the Lich King''s forces about to break through. Vaelen won free, and his knights were broken out of the cages across Jotunheim; with them, the vault can hold the line, for now.', 'quests 12949, 12951, 13085, 12982 descriptions and reward text'),
(21042, 1, 0, 255, 'Papers seized in the chaos of the Ebon Blade''s assault on the Weeping Quarry named the saronite''s destination: Malykriss, the Vile Hold. Keritose read it as wounded pride. Arthas did not take the loss of his death knights well, he said, and the boy is not used to losing.', 'quest 13174 description and reward text'),
(21042, 2, 0, 255, 'From the Rise of Suffering, Vereth the Cunning sent a captured stalker to scout Malykriss and found more death knights still loyal to Arthas than he had thought. The Lich King is sparing nothing to replace Acherus and the knights he lost with it, and a citadel of pure saronite would be hard to destroy. The Ebon Blade means not to destroy it, but to halt the work and cut down the new order''s leaders before they become a real threat.', 'quests 13155, 13143, 13145 descriptions and reward text'),
(21042, 3, 0, 255, 'The leaders fell one by one. The three riders of the Host of Suffering, Rokir of the unholy arts, sweet-smiling Sapph of frost and the brutal vrykul Baelok of blood, were slain, and then their true leader. Orbaz Bloodbane, self-proclaimed hand of the Lich King and an Arthas want-to-be in Vereth''s words, died at the lip of the pit beneath the citadel, with Mograine there to see it.', 'quests 13161, 13162, 13163 descriptions and reward text; quest 13164 description, request and reward text; creature_text 31283, 31290'),
(21043, 1, 0, 255, 'The Alliance''s plans in Icecrown hinged on taking the first gate before the Horde could, and the secret attack on Mord''rethar ended as a rout on the Broken Front, with the Horde upon it. Bartlett has sworn the Horde will pay without mercy and readies his people for a war on two fronts.', 'quest 13231 description and reward text; quests 13232, 13233'),
(21043, 2, 0, 255, 'Thassarian keeps his eyes on the real mission. He has drawn up tactics for every gate on the road: abominations turned against the defenders of the Death Gate, the Cult''s own disguises turned against it at the Desolation Gate, and an acid to keep the skeletal reavers before the Horror Gate from rising again once they fall.', 'quests 13286-13289, 13315, 13318, 13332, 13337, 13335 descriptions and reward text'),
(21044, 1, 0, 255, 'Korm heard about the Broken Front from a dying berserker: Horde troops on a reconnaissance had seen the Alliance assaulting the gate and fallen on them from behind. He laughed aloud. That, he said, is what it means to be Horde, and their boldness bought precious time, for without them the Alliance would likely hold the gate.', 'quest 13228 description and reward text'),
(21044, 2, 0, 255, 'Koltira keeps his attention on the real enemy while the sky-reaver nurses his hatred of the Alliance. He has drawn up tactics for every gate on the road: abominations turned against the defenders of the Death Gate, the Cult''s own disguises used against it at the Desolation Gate, and an acid to keep the skeletal reavers before the Horror Gate from rising again.', 'quests 13237, 13264, 13351, 13352, 13366, 13306, 13329 descriptions and reward text'),
(21045, 1, 0, 255, 'The fuse burned far too fast. The blast hurt the Scourge badly, but it also threw one of the bombers down the pit into Naz''anak, the Forgotten Depths. There, beneath icy water, lay a pulsing organ sealed in ice that cut like a blade at a touch, and a boy''s voice warned that its owner would come looking for whoever had touched it.', 'quests 13262, 13263, 13271, 13275, 13282 and 13388-13392 descriptions and reward text'),
(21045, 2, 0, 255, 'The boy, Matthias Lehner, showed the rest in visions until there was no doubt: the frozen organ was the heart of Arthas, cast down the pit when he became king. Their death knight adviser had heard the tale before, but had never believed it more than a story. Now the news had to go in secret to Tirion Fordring, whose Crusade alone could be trusted free of the Cult.', 'quests 13361, 13362, 13400, 13401 reward text; quests 13363, 13402 descriptions (rumors among the death knights; the Argent Crusade free of infiltration)'),
(21045, 3, 0, 255, 'A Cult procession carried the heart from the citadel to the Cathedral of Darkness, and Tirion went to meet it in disguise with a handful of hooded crusaders. The Lich King himself came. Tirion struck the heart with the Ashbringer and was struck down in turn, and only the Ebon Blade''s arrival brought his party out. He called it no failure: he had looked into the heart, and there is no Arthas Menethil anymore, only the Lich King.', 'quests 13364, 13403 description and reward text; creature_text 32239, 32184, 32241, 32310-32312; zone_icecrown.cpp npc_tirions_gambit_tirion'),
(21046, 1, 0, 255, 'An aspirant who bests an Argent valiant in the Aspirants'' Ring earns the rank of valiant and joins a capital city''s delegation, training under its grand champion and sparring with other valiants for a place in the grand melee.', 'quests 13679, 13680 description and reward text; quests 13684, 13699 (delegation under the grand champion; the valiant''s challenge)'),
(21046, 2, 0, 255, 'New champions are welcomed by Eadric the Pure, grand champion of the Argent Crusade, who at the Highlord''s request coordinates their training and the defense of the grounds, and by Crok Scourgebane of the Ebon Blade, who would show the paladins what real battle has made of his knights. Even between bouts, champions ride out against the Cult of the Damned across Icecrown.', 'quests 13794, 13795 description and reward text; quests 13789, 13791, 13682, 13788 (champions against the Cult)'),
(21046, 3, 0, 255, 'With the coliseum complete, the Silver Covenant and the Sunreavers vie with each other to serve the Argent Crusade by tending the beasts captured to fight in its arena: jormungar that grow strong on the eggs of their own kind, a raging magnataur that howls for its snobolds, and a yeti with a taste for shark meat.', 'quests 14076, 14090, 14112 descriptions and reward text; quests 14092, 14141, 14145 (the Sunreaver versions)'),
(21047, 1, 0, 255, 'The crystal told how three of them died: Lorien Sunblaze by poison, Sir Wendell Balfour burned alive, Conall Irongrip by a coward''s strike. All three had sparred with the Black Knight and were to fight him. His squire Maloric, who went off each day as if to chop wood, carried the proof: poison, knives, torches and oil.', 'quest 13643 description and reward text; quest 13654 description and reward text'),
(21047, 2, 0, 255, 'With an enchanted bridle lent by the Kirin Tor, the Black Knight''s own gryphon was made to carry a rider to its master''s home, and the orders found there settled who had sent him. The Black Knight is a member of the Cult of the Damned, sent by Arthas to disrupt the tournament.', 'quest 13663 description and reward text'),
(21047, 3, 0, 255, 'He was challenged in the light of day, where he could neither refuse nor murder in the dark, and he was defeated in the Ring of Champions. With his death, Rhydalla said, the tournament could serve its purpose again.', 'quest 13664 description and reward text'),
(21047, 4, 0, 255, 'Argent Confessor Paletress insisted that he receive a decent burial, but a dark presence lingered at his grave, and cultists carried the body off to Deathspeaker''s Watch. There the infamous Doctor Kohler reanimated and empowered him for the Lich King''s servants. What his master intends no one knows, and the tournament''s participants have been warned.', 'quest 14016 description and reward text; quest 14017 description and reward text');
